    <string name="setup_manual_home">This TV has no shortcut to that page. With the remote: Settings → System (or Device Preferences) → Accessibility → TV Home → turn it on. Or run the setup script from a phone once, which does it for you.</string>
    <string name="setup_manual_updates">This TV has no shortcut to that page. With the remote: Settings → Apps → Security &amp; restrictions → Unknown sources → TV Home → allow. Or run the setup script from a phone once, which does it for you.</string>
    <string name="setup_manual_default">This TV doesn\'t let you choose a home screen. That\'s fine: the Home button step already makes TV Home open on Home and at start-up.</string>
    <string name="ss_title">Set up on this TV</string>
    <string name="ss_hero">No phone needed</string>
    <string name="ss_hero_line">Turn on two settings with the remote, then press Set everything up. TV Home does the rest itself.</string>
    <string name="ss_step_dev">1. Turn on Developer options</string>
    <string name="ss_step_dev_value">About → press OK 7 times on the build</string>
    <string name="ss_step_debug">2. Turn on USB debugging</string>
    <string name="ss_debug_on">On</string>
    <string name="ss_debug_off">Developer options → USB debugging</string>
    <string name="ss_step_go">3. Set everything up</string>
    <string name="ss_go_ready">Ready</string>
    <string name="ss_go_wait">After steps 1 and 2</string>
    <string name="ss_manual">Open Settings with the remote: System (or Device Preferences) → About → press OK 7 times on "Android TV OS build" (or "Build"). Then back in System → Developer options → turn on USB debugging (on some TVs: Network or ADB debugging).</string>
